Subject: [PATCH] arm64: turn the zstd build feature on

Every package HaikuPorts builds is zstd-compressed, ca_root_certificates
included. build/jam/BuildFeatures enables zstd only when zstd_devel is
available, and the arm64 bootstrap package list has no zstd at all, so the
feature was silently off: packagefs, libbe and the boot loader were built
without ZstdCompressionAlgorithm, and a zstd package installed into
/boot/system/packages was never activated and said nothing about it. That
is why the root certificates never reached /boot/system/data/ssl.

This lists zstd, zstd_devel and the zstd source package under HaikuPorts'
names and versions. They are not on HaikuPorts for arm64: the binaries are
cross-built by haiku-rwebpositive-arm64's package-zstd-arm64.sh, and the
source package is HaikuPorts' own architecture-"source" file. All three are
in ../packages/ and add-media-arm64.sh copies them into the generated
directory's download/ when it is given one.

Note that jam does not track preprocessor defines: in a tree that was
already built with the feature off, delete the objects of packagefs,
kits/support, kits/package, bin/package, the boot loader's packagefs and
boot libs, and kits/libbe.so before rebuilding, or they keep their old
builds.

diff --git a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64 b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
index 85ff062d54..c0ebfd501b 100644
--- a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
+++ b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@ RemotePackageRepository HaikuPorts
 	texinfo-7.2_bootstrap-1
 	zlib-1.2.13_bootstrap-1
 	zlib_devel-1.2.13_bootstrap-1
+	# Not in HaikuPorts for arm64; cross-built under HaikuPorts' names so the
+	# zstd build feature turns on. Without it packagefs cannot read a
+	# zstd-compressed package, which is what every HaikuPorts package is.
+	zstd-1.5.6-2
+	zstd_devel-1.5.6-2
 	:
 	# source packages
 	bash
@@ -66,6 +71,7 @@ RemotePackageRepository HaikuPorts
 	sed
 	texinfo
 	zlib
+	zstd
 	:
 	# debuginfo packages
 	;
